  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Arts &amp; Culture: Culture Connects</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Culture Connects is one of the Global Programmes through which the British Council delivers its grant-funded activity. Approximately three quarters of this Global Programme consists of ODA eligible activity and outcomes and therefore funded from the British Council&#x2019;s ODA allocation.Culture Connects provides opportunities for the UK&#x2019;s arts and cultural professionals and organisations to foster long term relationships with their international peers and audiences by enabling connection and networking, providing intelligence, and facilitating creative collaboration, showcasing and touring. Embedding mutuality in programme design is essential to ensuring ODA eligibility for Culture Connects work and we have successfully developed ODA-eligible models for this work.There are four areas of focus for the programme: 1. Connecting Cultural Professionals, 2. Creative Collaboration, 3. Showcasing and Touring, 4. Digital Packages: &#x25fc; 1. Connecting Cultural Professionals: Inbound and outbound delegations and scoping trips, supporting collaborative R&amp;D, opportunities to expand industry networks, brokering relationships between UK and global arts and culture professionals, research and insight to inform markets.&#x25fc; 2. Creative Collaboration: Projects which enable meaningful collaboration between the UK arts sector and their international peers with mutual benefit. Enhances skills and knowledge in international working and cultural understanding.&#x25fc; 3. Showcasing and Touring: Sharing UK arts and culture work to audiences in countries and vice versa. &#x25fc; 4. Digital Packages: Curated or off the shelf touring digital packages to share UK and global work with audiences on digital platforms.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="3">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The audiences for this programme are: &#x25fc; Arts audiences&#x25fc; Artists &#x25fc; Art sector organisations</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&#x25fc;  1. Audiences internationally have a greater engagement with, and favourability towards, UK Arts, culture and creativity&#x25fc;  2. Supports the development of environmentally sustainable practice and international engagement.&#x25fc; 3. Learning and insights on current issues and trends are shared.&#x25fc; 4. Improve visibility, recognition and influence of women, disabled and other underrepresented creative professionals&#x25fc; 5. The UK&apos;s Arts, Culture and Creative sectors are better connected internationally, extending their profile and audiences.&#x25fc; 6. The UK Arts, Culture and Creative sectors have increased skills and networks to work internationally.</narrative>
  </description>
